Definition:
  LeanWang.Abstract.CoREHard is
    the function mapping an implicit element α of Type u_1 and an instance of typeclass Primcodable α and a function p from α to Prop to
      for every function q from ℕ to Prop where q is CoRE:
        there is a function r from ℕ to α such that
          r is computable and
          (for every natural number n:
            n is q if and only if (r n) is p).

Abbreviation:
  TranslationTiling.Abstract.Point is
    the function mapping a natural number d to
      the type of functions from indices in [0, d) to ℤ.

Abbreviation:
  TranslationTiling.Abstract.Prototile is
    the function mapping a natural number d to
      the type of lists of (Point d) elements.

Definition:
  TranslationTiling.Abstract.Adjacent is
    (the function mapping an implicit natural number d and an element p of Point d and an element q of Point d to
      the sum over indices i in [0, d) of |p i - q i| = 1).

Definition:
  TranslationTiling.Abstract.Connected is
    the function mapping an implicit natural number d and an element P of Prototile d to
      for every x ∈ P:
        for every y ∈ P:
          x is related to y by the reflexive transitive closure of
            (the function mapping an element p of Point d and an element q of Point d to
                p ∈ P and q ∈ P and (p and q are Adjacent)).

Definition:
  TranslationTiling.Abstract.Tiles is
    the function mapping an implicit natural number d and an element P of Prototile d to
      there is a set T of (Point d) elements such that
        for every element x of (Point d):
          there is a unique element t of (Point d) such that
            t ∈ T and x - t ∈ P.

Theorem TranslationTiling.Abstract.tiling_coRE_complete:
  for every natural number d where 3 ≤ d:
    (the function mapping an element P of Prototile d to
      P is Connected and P is Tiles) is LeanWang.Abstract.CoREComplete

Theorem TranslationTiling.Abstract.tiling_undecidable:
  for every natural number d where 3 ≤ d:
    (the function mapping an element P of Prototile d to
      P is Connected and P is Tiles) is not computable

Theorem TranslationTiling.Abstract.tiling_reduction:
  for every natural number d where 3 ≤ d:
    there is a function f from lists of LeanWang.Abstract.Tile elements to Prototile d such that
      f is computable and
      (for every list T of LeanWang.Abstract.Tile elements:
        f T ≠ [] and
        (f T) is Connected and
        (T is LeanWang.Abstract.TilesPlane if and only if (f T) is Tiles) and
        the length of (f T) as a real number ≤
          (the length of T as a real number + 4) ^
            (10 ^ 61 * log base 2 of (log base 2 of (the length of T as a real number + 4))))

Abbreviation:
  TranslationTiling.Abstract.RealPoint is
    the function mapping a natural number d to
      EuclideanSpace ℝ (the type of indices in [0, d)).

Definition:
  TranslationTiling.Abstract.Solid is
    the function mapping an implicit natural number d and an element P of Prototile d to
      the set of elements x of RealPoint d such that
        there is an element p of (Point d) such that
          p ∈ P and
          (for every index i in [0, d):
            p i as
                (the function mapping an index in [0, d) to
                      ℝ)
                  i ≤
              x.ofLp i and
            x.ofLp i ≤
              p i as
                  (the function mapping an index in [0, d) to
                        ℝ)
                    i +
                1).

Abbreviation:
  TranslationTiling.Abstract.Motion is
    the function mapping a natural number d to
      RealPoint d ≃ᵃⁱ[ℝ] RealPoint d.

Definition:
  TranslationTiling.Abstract.allMotions is
    the function mapping an implicit natural number d to
      the set of all elements of (Motion d).

Definition:
  TranslationTiling.Abstract.translations is
    (the function mapping an implicit natural number d to
      the set of elements f of Motion d such that
        f.linear = 1).

Definition:
  TranslationTiling.Abstract.translationsAndRotations is
    (the function mapping an implicit natural number d to
      the set of elements f of Motion d such that
        (LinearEquiv.det : (RealPoint d ≃ₗ[ℝ] RealPoint d) → ℝˣ) f.linear = 1).

Definition:
  TranslationTiling.Abstract.translationsAndReflections is
    the function mapping an implicit natural number d to
      the set of elements f of Motion d such that
        there is an element t of (Motion d) such that
          t ∈ translations and
          (there is an element p of (RealPoint d) such that
            there is an element q of (RealPoint d) such that
              f = t * EuclideanGeometry.reflection (AffineSubspace.perpBisector p q)).

Definition:
  TranslationTiling.Abstract.RealTiles is
    the function mapping an implicit natural number d and an element P of Prototile d and a set motions of (Motion d) elements to
      there is a set T of (Motion d) elements such that
        T ⊆ motions and
        (for almost every element x of (RealPoint d):
          there is a unique element f of (Motion d) such that
            f ∈ T and x ∈ the image of (Solid P) under f).

Theorem TranslationTiling.Abstract.real_tiling_coRE_hard:
  for every natural number d where 3 ≤ d:
    for every set motions of (Motion d) elements where translations ⊆ motions:
      (the function mapping an element P of Prototile d to
        P is Connected and (P and motions are RealTiles)) is LeanWang.Abstract.CoREHard

Theorem TranslationTiling.Abstract.real_tiling_undecidable:
  for every natural number d where 3 ≤ d:
    for every set motions of (Motion d) elements where translations ⊆ motions:
      (the function mapping an element P of Prototile d to
        P is Connected and (P and motions are RealTiles)) is not computable

Theorem TranslationTiling.Abstract.real_tiling_coRE_complete:
  for every natural number d where 3 ≤ d:
    for every motions ∈ ({allMotions, translations, translationsAndRotations, translationsAndReflections} : Set (Set (Motion d))):
      (the function mapping an element P of Prototile d to
        P is Connected and (P and motions are RealTiles)) is LeanWang.Abstract.CoREComplete

Theorem TranslationTiling.Abstract.real_tiling_reduction:
  for every natural number d where 3 ≤ d:
    there is a function f from lists of LeanWang.Abstract.Tile elements to Prototile d such that
      f is computable and
      (for every list T of LeanWang.Abstract.Tile elements:
        f T ≠ [] and
        (f T) is Connected and
        (T is LeanWang.Abstract.TilesPlane if and only if (f T) is Tiles) and
        ((f T) is Tiles if and only if (f T) and (translations) are RealTiles) and
        the length of (f T) as a real number ≤
          (the length of T as a real number + 4) ^
            (10 ^ 61 * log base 2 of (log base 2 of (the length of T as a real number + 4))))

Theorem TranslationTiling.Abstract.rigid_tiling_reduction:
  for every natural number d where 3 ≤ d:
    there is a function f from lists of LeanWang.Abstract.Tile elements to Prototile d such that
      f is computable and
      (for every list T of LeanWang.Abstract.Tile elements:
        f T ≠ [] and
        (f T) is Connected and
        (T is LeanWang.Abstract.TilesPlane if and only if (f T) is Tiles) and
        (for every set motions of (Motion d) elements where translations ⊆ motions:
          (f T) is Tiles if and only if (f T) and motions are RealTiles) and
        the length of (f T) as a real number ≤
          2 ^ (10 * (d + 1) ^ 2) *
            (the length of T as a real number + 4) ^
              (10 ^ 61 * log base 2 of (log base 2 of (the length of T as a real number + 4))))

Theorem TranslationTiling.Abstract.rigid_tiling_reduction_three:
  there is a function f from lists of LeanWang.Abstract.Tile elements to Prototile 3 such that
    f is computable and
    (for every list T of LeanWang.Abstract.Tile elements:
      f T ≠ [] and
      (f T) is Connected and
      (T is LeanWang.Abstract.TilesPlane if and only if (f T) is Tiles) and
      (for every set motions of (Motion 3) elements where translations ⊆ motions:
        (f T) is Tiles if and only if (f T) and motions are RealTiles) and
      the length of (f T) as a real number ≤
        64000 *
          (the length of T as a real number + 4) ^
            (10 ^ 61 * log base 2 of (log base 2 of (the length of T as a real number + 4))))
